# CODEOWNERS — review requirements for security-critical paths.
#
# GitHub auto-requests review from the owner when a PR touches a matching
# path, and (with "Require review from Code Owners" enabled in the branch
# ruleset) blocks merge until that owner approves.
#
# In this solo project the owner is the repo owner. The point is to
# demonstrate separation-of-duties: in a team, these paths would be owned
# by a security team distinct from the engineers writing Terraform, so
# suppression and policy changes get an independent reviewer.
#
# NOTE: the "Require review from Code Owners" ruleset toggle is left OFF
# here. GitHub forbids self-approval, so with a single owner it would make
# these files unmergeable. It would be switched on once a second reviewer
# exists, turning these requests into hard merge blocks.
#
#   - .checkov.yaml          system-wide Checkov suppressions (security policy)
#   - bootstrap/github_oidc.tf  OIDC trust + IAM roles that gate AWS access
#   - .github/CODEOWNERS      this file itself
.checkov.yaml                   @patrick-anderson-555
bootstrap/github_oidc.tf        @patrick-anderson-555
